(7722343, 1270870, 75585, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Paul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ErinKirsten:</b></div><hr/><i> I appreciate the perspective I just think it is oversaturated </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree completely. I did try reducing the saturation but I then lost contrast - I''ve tried again since and find that if only I''d reduced ''vibrancy'' rather than ''saturation'', that would have done the trick. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Either way, it is a very interesting stop and think perspective, well done!</td>', 'Originally posted by Paul: Originally posted by ErinKirsten: I appreciate the perspective I just think it is oversaturated   I agree completely. I did try reducing the saturation but I then lost contrast - I''ve tried again since and find that if only I''d reduced ''vibrancy'' rather than ''saturation'', that would have done the trick.   Either way, it is a very interesting stop and think perspective, well done!', '2022-06-29 12:43:34.000000', NULL, 0),
